@startuml sequence-diagram
title {{Scenario name}} — Scenario Walkthrough (optional, Model stage)

' ============================================================
' Optional tactical artifact (Vernon, Implementing Domain-Driven Design).
' Purpose: validate aggregate boundaries against ONE key scenario.
'
' THE RULE a DDD-valid sequence diagram obeys
' (Vernon, IDDD — aggregate rules of thumb #3 & #4):
'   WITHIN one aggregate   -> synchronous method calls. One transaction.
'   ACROSS aggregates      -> NEVER a direct call. The root publishes a
'                             DOMAIN EVENT (past tense) onto the broker;
'                             the other aggregate's POLICY reacts to it
'                             asynchronously, in its OWN transaction.
'   One transaction modifies exactly ONE aggregate.
'
' A step that calls Aggregate B from inside Aggregate A is a rule-#4
' VIOLATION -- fix it by splitting at the boundary (publish an event,
' subscribe a policy). Don't soften it; the diagram exists to expose these.
' ============================================================

skinparam maxMessageSize 160
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor Black
  ParticipantBorderColor Black
  ParticipantBackgroundColor White
  LifeLineBorderColor Gray
  LifeLineBackgroundColor WhiteSmoke
}

actor "Customer" as Customer

box "Order Aggregate\n(1 consistency boundary = 1 transaction)" #LightYellow
  participant "OrderAppService" as App
  participant "Order\n(root)"    as Order
end box

' The broker is the ONLY thing permitted to cross an aggregate boundary.
queue "Message Broker\n(domain / integration events)" as Broker #WhiteSmoke

box "Inventory Aggregate\n(its own transaction)" #White
  participant "ReservationPolicy\n(reacts to OrderPlaced)" as InvPolicy
  participant "Inventory\n(root)"                          as Inventory
end box

box "Shipping Aggregate\n(its own transaction)" #White
  participant "ShippingPolicy\n(reacts to OrderConfirmed)" as ShipPolicy
end box

' ============ WITHIN the Order aggregate: synchronous, one transaction ============
Customer -> App : place(customerId, items)
activate App
App      -> Order : **place**(customerId, items)
activate Order
Order    --> App : ok  ' invariants enforced here; OrderPlaced saved WITH the aggregate
deactivate Order
App      -> Broker : publish(**OrderPlaced**)   ' after commit (outbox)
deactivate App

' ============ ACROSS aggregates: ALWAYS via the broker, NEVER a direct call ============
Broker   -> InvPolicy : OrderPlaced
activate InvPolicy
note right of InvPolicy
  A separate transaction. Inventory sees
  only the event's public facts -- never
  Order's internals.
end note
InvPolicy -> Inventory : reserve(orderId, items)
activate Inventory
Inventory --> InvPolicy : ok
deactivate Inventory
InvPolicy -> Broker : publish(**StockReserved** / **StockShort**)
deactivate InvPolicy

' A later event still crosses the boundary via the broker, not a call.
Broker -> ShipPolicy : OrderConfirmed
activate ShipPolicy
ShipPolicy -> Broker : schedule(orderId)
deactivate ShipPolicy

' ============================================================
' Legend
'   solid arrow  -> a call or a broker message
'   dashed arrow -> a reply / a published event emerging from a root
'   box          -> an aggregate = ONE consistency boundary = ONE transaction
'   queue        -> the ONLY channel allowed to cross an aggregate boundary
'   **bold**     -> a domain event name (past tense, ubiquitous language)
' ============================================================

@enduml
